+## Bitbucket Cloud and several forge accounts
+
+**Bitbucket Cloud** is a forge like the others for a local project: issues and pull request views, Bitbucket Pipelines in the CI loop, and the task's PR opened by the backend. Its token is encrypted in `.workpilot/.env`, masked to the interface, and only ever sent to api.bitbucket.org. Design: [bitbucket.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/bitbucket.md).
+
+**Several accounts per forge**: GitHub, GitLab, Azure DevOps and Bitbucket accounts are registered once for the app, tokens encrypted in the main process, and each project names its own in its `.workpilot/.env`. Each project reads its issues, PRs and pipelines from the repository of its own git remotes; an empty repository, or one that is none of the remotes, is flagged with the right one a click away. Design: [forge-accounts.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/forge-accounts.md), [forge-repositories.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/forge-repositories.md).
