+## A microVM per task (optional)
+
+Off by default, in **Settings → Sandbox**: each task can run in a Docker Sandboxes microVM (`sbx`) with its own kernel and Docker engine, only its worktree mounted and the network closed to the allowlist. The agent CLIs run inside it with sbx's own keys, Settings shows sbx's status, and the VM is purged with the worktree. It is also what isolates an agent's commands on Windows 11. Design: [os-sandbox.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/os-sandbox.md).
+
+## Approval tiers for pull requests
+
+Each pull request gets a tier read without a model, from its kind, the layers and sensitive paths it touches, its size, its CI and the cross review: **N0** and **N1** merge on their own once everything is green, **N2** and **N3** wait for a person. The tiers start in observe mode; the `approvals` section of `workpilot.policy.yaml` can only make them stricter, and a task's sandbox and refused hosts count among the facts. Dependabot and Renovate PRs take an **express lane** through the same engine, with no task and no model: a green N0 merges at the head that was judged, only when the switch is on. Design: [approval-tiers.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/approval-tiers.md), [express-lane.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/express-lane.md).
