+### Working fast on the board
+
+- **Card colours**: each card takes the colour of its type (14 types in 5 families: feature, bug fix, refactoring, security…), read from its kind, category, severity and origin, nothing to fill in; a preview opens after 700 ms on hover. A finished card shows the agents' time, tokens and cost, who created it and who started it.
+- **Quick add** from Planning, Queue and In Progress: one card per pasted line; « + » in In Progress creates the card and starts it.
+- **Right-click** on a card or a column: the same actions as « ⋮ » (Type ▸, Priority ▸, Edit…). **Ctrl/Shift** click and Ctrl+A select several cards for bulk actions, and a whole selection drags at once; a delete waits a few seconds and Ctrl+Z takes it back; F2 renames in place, the arrow keys move between cards and Ctrl+/ shows the keys.
+- **Column bands**: each header is tinted with the column's colour, with a big count, a capacity gauge (In Progress slots, WIP limit) that turns amber, and a one-line summary you can hide.
+- **Before the first start**, the machine is checked (git, a first commit, the account) and a short card is read once by the AI, which may ask up to three questions; it never blocks the start.
+
+Design: [kanban-quick-edit.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-quick-edit.md), [kanban-card-colors.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-card-colors.md), [kanban-columns.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-columns.md), [task-readiness.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/task-readiness.md).
+
+### Ask the board
+
+Ask a question in any language (« has the CSV export already been done? ») and get every related ticket, with the roadmap, the ideas and the merged changes. The selected provider's model translates the question into the board's languages, words (BM25) and meaning (an embeddings model, local first) rank the candidates, and the model judges what the answer covers; without a model the ranking answers alone. « Check an idea » tells a product owner whether a planned feature is already there. It works on a local board, on a team server's board from the desktop, and in the mobile app. Design: [board-ask.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/board-ask.md).
+
+### Where the long suites run
+
+Before a full QA review, the app decides without a model where the project's full suite runs: on this machine, on the forge's CI from the task's branch pushed without a PR (GitHub Actions, Azure Pipelines, GitLab CI, Bitbucket Pipelines, Jenkins), or on the WorkPilot server, from the free CPU, RAM, GPU and VRAM and the suite's measured load; with no room, the suite queues, it is never skipped. The touched tests run first, a card's own choice wins over the project's, the merge waits while the CI runs, and after a merge the other green cards take the new base and run again. Design: [test-placement.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/test-placement.md), [suite-base-refresh.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/suite-base-refresh.md).
